<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21603" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γάνῠμαι</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, mostly pres.;
			impf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγάνυντο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Q.S.
					5.652
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγάνυτο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Or.</u>
					1.8c
				</span></i>
			: 
				Ep.
			
			fut.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γανύσσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					14.504
				</span></i>
			: pf.
			part.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γεγανῡμένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Anacreont.</u>
					35.3
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Them.
				<u>Or.</u>
				13.177a
			</span></i>: plpf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγεγάνυσο</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				20.240d
			</span></i>, al.:—<i>brighten up, be glad</i> or
			<i>happy</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γάνυται φρένα</span> he
				<i>is glad</i> at heart, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				13.493
			</span></i>: c. dat., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δάμαρ ἀνδρὶ φίλῳ ἐλθόντι γανύσσεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					14.504
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				20.405
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				12.43
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				612
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γ. ἐπί τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IT</u>
					1239
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					970
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Cyc.</u>
				504
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ τοῦ λόγου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phdr.</u>
					234d
				</span></i>
			.—Freq. in later Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.36
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				56
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.1098f
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Polyaen.
				1.18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Or.</u>
				1.40b
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Them.
			</span></i> ll.cc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾄδων καὶ γανύμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aristid.
					<u>Or.</u>
					50(26).40
				</span></i>
			; freq. written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γανν-</span> in codd.
				(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γα-ν-υ-</span>from root <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γαυ-</span>, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γαίω,
				γαῦρος</span>.)</div>
